laurel 2157: the stage-1 SMMU check (2154) no longer turns the GPU off; its own GPU VA seed (no pool free, 2156).
Boot 07:19 (2154 + 2156): "LAUREL GPU POOL: free of 0x1000000+0xef000000 refused" (hw_start seeded the GPU VA allocator
through redwood_gpu_address_free = the pool's checked free in pass-through), then the stage-1 switch, the CP ring fetch at
VA 0xc0020040 faulted (terminated), the CP hung (rptr 17 wptr 21), the pass-through fallback found it stuck and the GPU
went off. Boot 07:21 with gpu_smmu=0: GPU on in pass-through (2154 + 2156 are fine there).
Changes:
- va_seed(): the allocator's one range 0x01000000-0x7fffffff, set directly when the tables come up; pass-through uses no
  allocator (no seed in hw_start, no refused free).
- the check: one line per step (LAUREL GPU SMMU: check 1..4): 1 the CP buffers walk to VA = PA in the tables (CPU-side
  walk of every page, each table link checked), 2 context bank 0 registers as held (with CBA2R0: FSR FORMAT 2 hints at
  a non-AArch64 walk), 3 a CP fence at VA = PA, 4 a CP fence to a kernel page at VA != PA. Linux's context bank values and
  order (CBA2R, CBAR type 1 + BPSHCFG NSH + MemAttr WB + VMID 1, TCR2 PASize 36 + AS + SEP upstream, TCR, TTBR0, MAIR0,
  SCTLR last).
- during the check a fault STALLS the access (SCTLR.CFCFG) instead of terminating it; the fault is logged decoded (FSR
  bits, FORMAT, FAR, FSYNR0 level/read-write/table walk, CPU-side walk of FAR) before anything clears it. On failure the
  context bank goes back to pass-through and a stalled access to our own memory at VA = PA (CP buffers, GPU pool) is
  retried there (CB_RESUME TnR 0): the CP goes on. Any other stalled access is terminated. In use (check passed): fault =
  terminate, as before.
- cp_recover(): CP idle: one fence. CP hung: GPU power collapse (power_up), zap resume (SCM set_remote_state 0, as Linux),
  SMMU pass-through again, CP start + fence test (A610: no RBBM_SW_RESET, Linux a6xx_gpu_sw_reset). The GPU stays ON in
  pass-through with 2150's backboardd-only rule. cp_start keeps the CP buffers on a second start (test va, not md).
- tables: 16 per 64 KiB pool unit (was one unit per PAGE_SIZE chunk).
Lines: LAUREL GPU SMMU: check 1: ... | check 2: ... | check 3: ... | check 4: ... | on: ... | check failed: <why>; context
bank 0 back to pass-through[, the stalled access retried there] | pass-through: the CP goes on ... | off: <why>: pass-through.
Kill switch: gpu_smmu=0 (as 2154). Docs: docs/laurel_sprout/gpu.md "SMMU stage 1".

